WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.767
Prosecutors say

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.769
the 21 year old Air National Guardsman

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.970
accused of leaking

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.072
highly sensitive military documents

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.040
on social media

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.008
was actually warned

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.509
repeatedly not to do that,

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.143
warn that he was

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.278
mishandling classified intelligence.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.448
Air Force memoranda detail three

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.683
separate instances

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.984
since September of Jack

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.486
to share his alleged misconduct.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.787
These new revelations come days

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.188
before a judge will determine

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.090
whether he stays behind bars

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.492
ahead of his trial or Natasha

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.559
Bertrand is following all of this

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.127
in the Pentagon.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:29.763
I could not believe I couldn't believe

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:30.864
this headline

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:31.464
when I read it

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.866
that there were multiple warnings.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:36.069
And so he had access to all of this.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:36.836
That's right, Poppy.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:37.937
So the first warning

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.407
apparently came in September of 20, 22

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.175
when his superiors actually saw him

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.344
taking notes on classified intelligence

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.879
and told him to stop.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:46.713
Now, the next warning

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.081
came in October

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.015
of 2022

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.418
where he was in a briefing, essentially,

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:54.587
and he was asking very deep questions,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:56.823
deep dove questions into intelligence,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:57.290
really,

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.092
that had nothing to do with his job.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:01.394
And the superiors there told him

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.095
that he needs

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:02.896
to really focus

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.097
on his actual duties,

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:06.433
which of course, were related to it.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.233
He was essentially

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:07.767
an IT

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.668
person for the Air

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.737
National Guard there in Massachusetts.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.504
And so there was essentially

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.972
a cease and desist order for him

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.874
to stop doing these deep dives

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.910
into this kind of intelligence.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:20.313
Then in January of 20, 23 of this year,

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.648
he was again

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.283
observed doing

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.284
these kind of deep dives

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.218
into intelligence.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.319
And he was warned again

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.720
by his superiors not to do it.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.922
It does not seem

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.590
like he was actually reprimanded

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.492
at that point by his commanders.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.494
But it was noted in these Air

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.862
National Guard memos

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.363
that he was looking at things

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.465
and looking at intelligence

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.166
that he was not supposed to be doing.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.401
And we should note that

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.435
the commanders

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.237
there actually offered him

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:45.271
a new position.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.639
If you wanted to

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.241
look into this intelligence more

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.643
if he wanted more kind of exposure to it

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.144
in a way

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.146
that actually comported with his duties.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.814
They offered to move him into a new job

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:55.748
that would allow him to do it.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.783
So instead of

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.218
really taking away his access

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.385
to this classified information

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:00.453
after three strikes

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.921
against him, essentially,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.755
they offered to simply

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.257
move him into a new job.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.558
Now, we did reach out to the Air

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.327
National Guard for comment.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.028
They said they cannot comment right now

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.897
because it is an ongoing investigation.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:12.265
But they did suspend

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.967
two commanders in his unit

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.336
pending the outcome of this investigation

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.271
and the entire intelligence mission

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.173
was actually taken away

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.040
from this unit

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.475
pending the completion

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.510
of the investigation.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.911
So we'll see how this shakes out

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.980
on Friday when he has his hearing

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.448
where a judge is going to determine

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:29.015
whether or not he's

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.083
going to stay behind bars.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.751
But prosecutors are arguing, look,

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:32.819
he needs to stay there

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.453
because clearly

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.054
he has a disregard here

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.222
for this kind of classified

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:37.824
and national security information. Poppy.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.025
It's interesting how that would play

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.426
into the judge's decision.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.194
Clearly, Natasha,

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.428
thanks to the reporting.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.530
Here with more is CNN's

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.165
chief law enforcement and intelligence

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:46.533
analyst John Miller.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.167
John,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.902
learning this from federal prosecutors

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:49.435
as they're saying,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.970
there are these three incidences

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.139
where incidents where he was

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.741
writing notes on classified intelligence,

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.375
which is, you know,

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:55.875
you're not supposed to

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.277
do putting in his pocket

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.311
then he was looking

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:00.346
at a trove of information, deep diving,

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.247
they said,

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:04.117
and then he was looking at intelligence

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.452
that was not related to his primary duty

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.488
Why were those incidents not enough

00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.256
to remove him from his role?

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.858
They were enough.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.526
What didn't happen?

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.162
So what we're seeing now is that base

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:19.132
this is extraordinarily unusual.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:21.334
That base has been suspended

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.736
from its intelligence mission totally.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.973
The commanding officer has been suspended

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.840
from command of it,

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.176
as well as the executive officer.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.845
So in the Pentagon's review, clearly

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.747
they have recognized problems there

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.650
and basically shut that operation down

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.551
in terms

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.787
of the classified intelligence side.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:44.190
But the question is, he's making notes

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.925
of classified documents.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.427
We know from earlier

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.762
court filings that he

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.331
he was nervous about this

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.265
because he had been caught.

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.166
So he just started

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:55.034
taking the documents wholesale.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.236
The real answer is

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.437
have these three things

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.339
been treated seriously at the time?

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:00.473
This would have been a referral

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.207
to the base's

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.375
security officer

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.243
who was supposed to ensure

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.777
the security of those documents.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.845
And then logically,

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.247
it should have gone to an organization

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:08.147
like OCI,

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.516
the Office of Special Investigations,

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.418
which is the Air Force's

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.754
Criminal Investigation Bureau, to see

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.823
you know, one thing is one thing.

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.124
Two things, three things.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:20.293
He went to a classified briefing

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.328
and sat in the audience and asked

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.030
extraordinarily detailed questions

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.832
about things that nothing had

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.933
that had to do with his realm

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.268
and remember what his realm was.

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:29.936
He was the IT guy.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.570
His job was to

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.372
make sure the systems were working.

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.406
He wasn't an analyst.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.141
He wasn't a target or he wasn't a drone.

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:35.908
Pilot.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:36.876
So all of this

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:37.910
should have been setting off

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:38.911
alarm bells sooner.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.614
But should it also change writ large?

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:44.717
How how the Pentagon allows

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.085
people in what positions

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.287
just to have access

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.921
to classified documents.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:49.555
So that's something

00:04:49.555 --> 00:04:52.292
the Pentagon is looking at now, which is

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:54.494
the person

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:55.628
in that job,

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.163
who is basically the person

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.665
that makes the systems run,

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.133
actually needs to have

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.168
that needs to have that clearance

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:04.003
because you can't access them.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.672
You can't access the mechanics

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:06.572
of the system.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.641
Well, that information is contained

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.742
and not have been through

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.477
that background investigation.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.679
That also doesn't

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.680
mean, as you point out,

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.014
that you need to be looking at it

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.282
and reading it

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:17.150
because it has nothing

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:17.917
to do with your job

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.852
to make sure the system functions.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:22.021
So this is a holistic review about

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.623
where do you put up these fences.

00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:25.925
But to get back to Caitlin's question,

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:26.993
the real

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:27.694
the real thing is

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:29.295
we don't need to change all the rules.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.531
We we need to go by the rules

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.999
that were already in place

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.534
when alarm bells go off.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.769
That has to go up the chain further.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.670
And it did.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.872
And yet he stayed in his job.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:40.406
John Miller,

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:41.874
as you learn more, keep us updated.

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.209
Just remarkable developments, though.

